 "intro_html": "An <b>onigirazu</b> (“un-squeezed rice ball”) is the lazy cousin of <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri</a>: no shaping at all. Rice, filling and rice are stacked on a sheet of nori, the four corners fold in like an envelope, and one cut through the middle shows the layers. This is Just One Cookbook’s <b>ginger pork</b> build — her shogayaki, a crisp lettuce leaf and a drizzle of Kewpie — so every bite is juicy, sweet-salty and gingery. Make the pork first; the rice should be warm when you build.",
