 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Stir together in a small bowl:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>soy sauce <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span></span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sake (sauce) <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"2\">2 tbsp</span></span></li><li>sugar <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span></span></li></ul></li><li>Peel the ginger and grate it, keeping the juice. Squeeze out <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span> ginger juice</b>: half goes into the sauce, half is for the pork.</li><li>Add <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"2\" data-b=\"3\" data-s=\"0\">2–3 tsp</span> of the squeezed grated ginger to the sauce, to taste.</li><li>Grate <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tbsp</span></b> of the onion with its juice into the sauce. Keep the rest of the onion.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Ginger sauce",
