     },
     {
      "caption": "Ginger juice and sake over the pork, then a light dusting of flour.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigirazu/2-how2.webp?v=57c65c4653"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigirazu/2.webp?v=ca7a94c1b1",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Ginger pork",
   "part_id": "part-ginger-pork",
   "time": "~6 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~6 min</span>",
   "title": "Pork and onion",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"340\">340 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Thinly sliced pork loin"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sake (pork)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Plain flour"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat the oil in a large frying pan over <b>medium-high</b> heat.</li><li>Lay the pork in a single layer and turn each slice once the underside is golden. Work in batches — a crowded pan steams the meat.</li><li>As soon as it is no longer pink, move it to a plate. It finishes in the sauce.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium-high",
    "label_html": "<span>medium-high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Sear the pork",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Turn each slice once the underside is golden.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigirazu/3-how1.webp?v=f187d7eedf"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigirazu/3.webp?v=a231f9c6bf",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": "Ginger pork",
   "part_id": "part-ginger-pork",
   "time": "~6 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~6 min</span>",
   "title": "Sear the pork",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\">1–2 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Neutral oil"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>A little more oil if needed, then the sliced onion: cook on medium until golden and tender, 6–8 min.</li><li>Pork back in. Stir the sauce once more and pour it over.</li><li>Simmer, spooning the sauce over the pork, about 2 minutes until it thickens and coats. Pepper if you like.</li><li>Let it cool on a plate until just warm, about 5 minutes.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Onion, then the sauce",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pork back in, sauce over, spoon it over for about 2 minutes.",
      "src": "illustrations/onigirazu/4-how1.webp?v=d8f22265ba"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/onigirazu/4.webp?v=cc4da1f350",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": "Ginger pork",
   "part_id": "part-ginger-pork",
